# CODEOWNERS
#
# Integration support intake & triage (see docs/integrations/support-intake.md)
#
# Response ownership for consumer integration reports filed via the public
# intake path (GitHub issue form: .github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/integration-report.yml).
# Severity routing categories (S1-S4) are defined in the intake doc; the
# owners below are the default responders for each triage category.

# Default owners for everything in the repo.
*                                   @stellar-oracle/maintainers

# Integration support intake & triage ownership.
# S1 (critical / funds-at-risk) and S2 (major) reports are routed to the
# integrations maintainers; S3/S4 fall back to the default owners above.
/docs/integrations/                 @stellar-oracle/integrations
/.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/integration-report.yml  @stellar-oracle/integrations

# Supply-chain hardening (see docs/security/malware-incident-2026-10.md).
# Changes to anything that can execute code on a contributor's machine or in CI
# need a maintainer's review.
/.github/                           @stellar-oracle/maintainers
/.husky/                            @stellar-oracle/maintainers
/.devcontainer/                     @stellar-oracle/maintainers
/scripts/                           @stellar-oracle/maintainers
**/package.json                     @stellar-oracle/maintainers
**/package-lock.json                @stellar-oracle/maintainers
/.gitignore                         @stellar-oracle/maintainers
